        "name": "Convert from text to date",
        "generativeText": {
          "modelType": "anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5",
          "name": "acmeDobFormatted",
          "prompt": "You are a date-formatting utility inside a customer service application.\n\nTASK\nConvert the input value {acmeDob:NLX.Text}into a calendar date using the exact format YYYY-MM-DD (4-digit year, 2-digit month, 2-digit day, separated by hyphens).\n\nRULES\n- Interpret {acmeDob:NLX.Text}regardless of how it was provided (e.g., \"03151990\", \"March 15 1990\", \"15/03/1990\", \"1990-3-15\", March Fifteenth nineteen ninety).\n- Always zero-pad month and day to two digits and use the full 4-digit year.\n- If the day and month order is ambiguous, assume US order (month first).\n- Do not include any time, timezone, weekday, or extra text.\n- If {acmeDob:NLX.Text}cannot be interpreted as a valid date, output exactly: INVALID\n\nOUTPUT\nReturn only the converted date in YYYY-MM-DD format (or INVALID). No labels, no explanation, no punctuation.",
          "maxTokens": 4000,
          "temperature": 0.5
        }
      },
